              "type": "text",
              "text": "A class has a class monitor and 23 other students. From Monday to Friday, a different student is assigned to clean the whiteboard (no repeats within the week). The class monitor must be given one of the days. How many such five-day schedules are possible?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\binom{23}{4}\\times5!=1\\,062\\,600$ schedules.",
      "worked": "Choose four of the 23 other students, then arrange the five selected students across the five weekdays.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\binom{23}{4}\\times5!\\\\N&=8855\\times120\\\\N&=1\\,062\\,600.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
